{"ts": "2026-10-27T06:52:22.641307Z", "run_id": "r-20261027T0651Z-62b6", "unit": "openspec:proxy-data-plane-paths", "seq": 16, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-001", "id": "Q-001", "status": "answered", "reason": "The design phrases the item as conditional on service-token-files landing. I verified in the repository that it has not: it sits in openspec/changes (not archive), its proposal describes svcid.FromEnv as a new function, no FromEnv exists in packages/go/svcid, and the proxy config loader reads both tokens via getEnv with no _FILE form. The spec requirement for the page only requires the names in design.md's section list, which does not include token _FILE variables. Documenting them now would describe unshipped behaviour, so the answer is to leave them out and treat the note as a follow-up for the other change.", "called": true, "tasks": ["1.1", "2.1", "3.1", "4.1"], "target": null, "kind": "ambiguous", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 0.8679845, "decision": "answer", "answer_sha256": "b8b1d70f8d5466f819d6dd6ad8bec99573e1a6021583ae0e0a2410238701f54e", "checked": [{"ref": "spec:design.md", "quote": "If `service-token-files` lands after this change, its `*_FILE` variables should be added to the page's section 2.", "claim": "The design itself makes the addition conditional on the other change landing, so it is a follow-up for that change rather than work for this unit."}, {"ref": "spec:design.md", "quote": "**Keys and identities**: `MINTKEY_VAULT_KEK_FILE`, `MINTKEY_BROKER_SIGNING_KEY_FILE`; the proxy's vault identity", "claim": "Section 2's required list names only the two existing key-file variables and the token variables in their environment form, not token *_FILE variables."}, {"ref": "openspec/changes/service-token-files/proposal.md:17", "quote": "New function `svcid.FromEnv(name string) (string, error)` in the existing package `packages/go/svcid`: when", "claim": "service-token-files is still an unarchived proposal that describes the file-reading function as new, i.e. not yet implemented."}, {"ref": "apps/proxy-plugin/internal/config/config.go:72", "quote": "VaultIdentityToken: getEnv(\"MINTKEY_VAULT_PROXY_TOKEN\", \"\"),", "claim": "The proxy still reads its vault identity token only from the environment variable, with no *_FILE form in the code."}, {"ref": "apps/proxy-plugin/internal/config/config.go:69", "quote": "ProxyServiceToken:  getEnv(\"MINTKEY_PROXY_SERVICE_TOKEN\", \"\"),", "claim": "The proxy's service token is likewise read only from the environment, confirming service-token-files has not landed."}]}
